# The entailment regimes SPARQL 1.2 Entailment Regimes defines, as the
# service description vocabulary types them.
#
# Each regime's table in SPARQL 1.2 Entailment Regimes (§2 RDF, §4 RDFS,
# §5 D-Entailment, §6 OWL 2 RDF-Based Semantics, §7 OWL 2 Direct Semantics,
# §8.1 RIF Core) gives its IRI, "which can be used in the SPARQL 1.2 Service
# Description of a SPARQL endpoint", as the object of sd:defaultEntailmentRegime
# or sd:entailmentRegime (§1.4). Both properties have the range
# sd:EntailmentRegime (sparql-service-description.ttl), so each regime is an
# sd:EntailmentRegime (RDF 1.2 Semantics, rdfs3). The documents the regime IRIs
# dereference to (Entailment.ttl and one per regime) state only that each is an
# ent:Entailment; this document states the membership the SPARQL 1.2
# specifications give them.

@prefix ent: <http://www.w3.org/ns/entailment/> .
@prefix sd: <http://www.w3.org/ns/sparql-service-description#> .

# ent:RDF (§2) joins them once RDFTranslator can name an individual RDF; see
# Package.swift.
ent:RDFS a sd:EntailmentRegime .
ent:D a sd:EntailmentRegime .
ent:OWL-RDF-Based a sd:EntailmentRegime .
ent:OWL-Direct a sd:EntailmentRegime .
ent:RIF a sd:EntailmentRegime .
